      "text": "Showing 1 to 20 of 177 entries\n1\n2\n...\n9\nPortal Term\n\t\nDefinition\n\t\nExample / Usage\n\n\n\t\n\t\nInactive\n\t\nIndicates that a record, user, configuration, or process is no longer active or available for use.\n\t\nAn inactive contact is no longer used for current business activities.\n\n\nContract\n\t\nA legally binding agreement between parties defining terms, obligations, deliverables, and other conditions.\n\t\nA awarded government contract is stored and tracked in the portal.\n\n\nIntegration\n\t\nA connection between the portal and another application or external data source.\n\t\nThe portal integrates with an external government data source.\n\n\nAuthentication Provider\n\t\nExternal or internal service responsible for verifying user identity.\n\t\nAn organization's identity provider authenticates portal users.\n\n\nDashboard Metric\n\t\nA numerical or calculated value displayed on a dashboard.\n\t\nTotal Open Opportunities is a dashboard metric.\n\n\nAuthorization\n\t\nThe process of determining what an authenticated user is allowed to access or perform.\n\t\nAfter login, the system determines which modules the user can access.\n\n\nClose Date\n\t\nThe expected date on which an opportunity is expected to be won, lost, or otherwise concluded.\n\t\nThe expected award date is entered as the close date.\n\n\nAudit Trail\n\t\nHistorical record of changes or actions performed on a record or within the system.\n\t\nThe audit trail shows who changed an opportunity status and when.\n\n\nNon-Functional Requirement\n\t\nRequirement describing qualities or constraints such as performance, security, or availability.\n\t\nThe portal must meet defined response-time requirements.\n\n\nMaster Data\n\t\nCore business information shared or referenced across multiple processes or systems.\n\t\nAccount and customer information may be treated as master data.\n\n\nFunctional Requirement\n\t\nRequirement describing what the system should do.\n\t\nThe portal must allow users to create and edit opportunities.\n\n\nApproval Matrix\n\t\nRules defining who must approve a transaction or request based on specific conditions.\n\t\nHigh-value opportunities require multiple levels of approval.\n\n\nLead\n\t\nA potential business prospect that may be qualified for further engagement.\n\t\nA newly identified company is entered as a lead for follow-up.\n\n\nAccount\n\t\nAn organization or company represented in the portal.\n\t\nA government agency or commercial customer can be maintained as an account.\n\n\nWrite Access\n\t\nPermission allowing a user to create or modify information.\n\t\nA manager has write access to opportunity records.\n\n\nSupport Ticket\n\t\nA formal record used to track a reported problem, request, or service inquiry.\n\t\nA user creates a support ticket for a login problem.\n\n\nCreated Date\n\t\nDate and time when a record was created.\n\t\nThe Created Date indicates when an opportunity entered the system.\n\n\nRFI\n\t\nRequest for Information; a government request used to gather information from industry before a potential procurement.\n\t\nA company responds to an RFI to demonstrate its capabilities.\n\n\nChange Request\n\t\nFormal request to modify functionality, configuration, data, or system behavior.\n\t\nA business user submits a change request for a new field.\n\n\nTarget System\n\t\nSystem receiving data from another application or source.\n\t\nThe portal can act as the target system during data import.\nShow: \n20\n40\n60\n80\n100\n Entries\nJump To:\nGo\n1\n2\n...\n9",
